# Passkeys setup checklist (frontend)

> Generated by `php artisan auth:setup --frontend-path=…` (the light-it auth package). It
> lists what the package could not do for you, because it never edits your files. Tick
> each box, then **delete this file**. How passkeys work: `docs/passkeys.md` in the
> package.
>
> Signing in with a passkey skips the 2FA code: a passkey with user verification is already
> multi-factor. Password and Google sign-in still ask for it.

- [ ] **Install dependencies** (`{{ packageManager }}`): {{ dependencyReport }}
- [ ] **Add the "Sign in with passkey" button** in `src/routes/(public)/_guest/login/-components/login-form.tsx`:
  1. Add as the last import: `import { PasskeyLoginButton } from "./passkey-login-button";`
  2. Add `<PasskeyLoginButton />` on the line after the submit button's closing `</Button>` (the one
     showing `{t("login.login")}`)
- [ ] **Add the i18n keys** to `src/i18n/locales/en.json` (and translate them in `es.json`):
  the `passkeys` block at the top level and `navigation.links.passkeys` next to the existing
  `navigation.links` keys.

At the top level:

```json
"passkeys": {
  "title": "Passkeys",
  "description": "Passkeys let you sign in with your fingerprint, face or screen lock instead of a password.",
  "loading": "Loading your passkeys...",
  "loadError": "We couldn't load your passkeys. Reload the page to retry.",
  "empty": "You haven't added a passkey yet.",
  "createdAt": "Added {date}",
  "signIn": {
    "submit": "Sign in with passkey",
    "unsupported": "This browser or device can't sign in with a passkey."
  },
  "form": {
    "name": "Passkey name",
    "nameTooLong": "Use 100 characters or fewer."
  },
  "add": {
    "open": "Add passkey",
    "title": "Add a passkey",
    "description": "Name it after the device it lives on, then confirm with your password.",
    "submit": "Continue",
    "success": "Passkey added"
  },
  "rename": {
    "open": "Rename",
    "title": "Rename passkey",
    "description": "Pick a name that tells you which device this passkey is on.",
    "submit": "Save",
    "success": "Passkey renamed"
  },
  "delete": {
    "open": "Delete",
    "title": "Delete passkey",
    "description": "Enter your password to delete {name}. You won't be able to use it again.",
    "submit": "Delete",
    "success": "{name} was deleted"
  },
  "errors": {
    "cancelled": "The passkey request was cancelled or timed out.",
    "unsupported": "This browser or device can't create passkeys.",
    "misconfigured": "This site isn't set up for passkeys yet. Please contact support.",
    "alreadyRegistered": "This device already has a passkey for your account.",
    "challengeExpired": "That took too long. Try again.",
    "notRecognised": "This passkey isn't registered. Sign in with your password and add it again."
  }
}
```

Next to the existing `navigation.links` keys:

```json
"navigation": { "links": { "passkeys": "Passkeys" } }
```

- [ ] **Link the passkeys page from the sidebar** in `src/routes/_private/-components/sidebar/sidebar.tsx`,
  at the end of `links`:
  `{ path: "/account/passkeys", label: t("navigation.links.passkeys"), icon: <Icons.Lock /> },`

Check it worked: run `vite` once (`dev` or `build`) so the router adds `/account/passkeys`,
then `{{ packageManager }} exec tsc --noEmit` passes, the login shows **Sign in with passkey**,
and **Passkeys** shows in the sidebar.
